        "date": "2026-11-14T01:46:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): flip STEP faces deterministically; outward once per shell; say flips by name\n\nSecond review of PR #1576 (pullrequestreview-5900373722):\n- The orientation solve is deterministic: votes in an ordered map, boundary\n  segments and shells sorted, and the flips decided by a parity union-find\n  that joins face pairs strongest evidence first (exact shared edges, then\n  T-junction votes, then face numbers). 10208.STEP gave two flip sets over\n  three runs before.\n- Each connected group keeps the kernel's winding on its majority side;\n  outward is decided once, from the whole shell's signed volume, and only\n  when some face is flipped. A cavity wound inward and a lone curved face\n  keep their winding.\n- A shared edge still running the same way in both faces after the flips\n  is refused by name; a T-junction-only disagreement is said in the notes.\n- Flips are said by name in the import result: Graded::notes,\n  ImportModel::notes, the MCP/script import_model answer and the status\n  line. The gap width is measured over every gap edge (bounded work).\n\nRefs #1573\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
